/-! # THRTAIL T-A1: the THR dimension stage `NumsXT2`, part 1: the THR load term

The THR writer shell is dimensioned by `n' = 2^(m_T)`, `m_T = mOfT K_L P + T`, `T = K_f·C_D·((k' + L)²·d + k' + L²)`,
`d = (⌈√(B_T·L)⌉ + 1 + L²)·C_D` (THRU4's `Ψ_T = C_D((k+L)²·C_D(√(B_T·L) + L²) + k + L²)`, P3:3094-3107, with
`k' = r·natBitLength(n/r + 1) ∈ [k, 2k]` and `⌈√·⌉ + 1 ≥ sqrtUp`). This file computes `T` in the dimension stage's
32 registers from `n` (the SYM stage `NumsXS`'s generator at the THR op list):

* `qAW`, **`qA_run`** (the star numbers, the sparse count, the mode bit, the THR cap `B_T`: `StarNums`, `SparseNum`,
  `CapNum` at `.thr`);
* `qBW`, **`qB_run`** (`n/r` (`SymDec.div1`), `natBitLength` (`FiltNum.bitLen1`), `k'`, `B_T·L`, `⌈√·⌉`
  (`LevelW.sqrtW`), `L²`, `d`, `(k'+L)²`, the products (`mulByW`, `mulAddW`), `T` into `rF` (`20`));
* `qCW`, **`qC_run`** (every register but `n` and `T` cleared); `qA_vals`, `qB_vals`, `qC_vals`.

Paper quantity of the main type: the THR load `Ψ_T` (P3:3094-3107), which sizes the THR writer's dimension. -/

